 :residual-risk
 "One layer is blocked (as-float) and it is REACHED by this component, so the
  port is partial: Transaction.amount does not store what aadhaar.main stores
  for three of five probed inputs. Do not read the com-aave record across to
  this repo on that point.

  Four of the six entities (Consent, Transaction, Document,
  VerificationRequest) were not driven end to end through the handlers; the
  table, refs and route hashes cover all six, but the float arm in particular
  was probed directly and NOT through handle-create on a Transaction.

  The as-float refusal is a NATIVE-TARGET refusal. kotoba-script web and typed
  Wasm are named by the refusal itself as targets that carry typed values and
  were not tried, so this may not be a language gap at all.

  Re-run q9-probes/ after any amu frontend OR BACKEND landing -- the 2026-09-03
  record said 'frontend' and that was too narrow: the two things that block
  this component now are both backend refusals of modules the frontend admits."}
